00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:02,189
Nika OS hatch, by BCUB3:

2
00:00:02,189 --> 00:00:07,853
an agent that specializes on its user's own work, inside a per-tenant frame.

3
00:00:07,853 --> 00:00:12,176
Built during the Meta hackathon, on Muse Glimmer thirty B.

4
00:00:13,376 --> 00:00:13,940
Context:

5
00:00:13,940 --> 00:00:17,397
at BCUB3 this pattern already runs in production.

6
00:00:17,397 --> 00:00:21,419
Today we rebuilt its core loop from scratch, in the open.

7
00:00:24,343 --> 00:00:26,182
First, the isolation tests:

8
00:00:26,182 --> 00:00:30,743
each tenant has its own memory, and cross-tenant reads are refused.

9
00:00:33,871 --> 00:00:35,660
Now the agent at work:

10
00:00:35,660 --> 00:00:42,084
a CPU replay of our real GPU run, with the exact outputs Muse Glimmer produced.

11
00:00:42,334 --> 00:00:48,265
Each task becomes a trajectory, with its memory sources, its verdict and four trace IDs.

12
00:00:48,515 --> 00:00:51,477
A bottleneck is measured, so the tenant hatches:

13
00:00:51,477 --> 00:00:53,699
a benchmark is pre-registered first.

14
00:00:53,949 --> 00:00:56,745
These are the real GPU training logs.

15
00:00:56,745 --> 00:01:00,221
First, a negative control on shuffled answers.

16
00:01:05,054 --> 00:01:06,797
The paired test rejects it.

17
00:01:06,797 --> 00:01:07,572
Rolled back.

18
00:01:18,432 --> 00:01:22,026
The real adapter wins forty three items and loses none.

19
00:01:22,026 --> 00:01:22,614
Promoted.

20
00:01:43,204 --> 00:01:44,586
The consulting firm:

21
00:01:44,586 --> 00:01:46,315
ninety wins, zero losses.

22
00:01:46,315 --> 00:01:46,937
Promoted.

23
00:01:47,187 --> 00:01:53,950
Each tenant is then served with its own adapter only, and a memory file moved to another tenant
is refused.

24
00:01:54,850 --> 00:01:55,610
The numbers.

25
00:01:55,610 --> 00:02:04,855
On one hundred held out requests, the machine shop goes from fifty seven to one hundred
percent, and the consulting firm from five to ninety five.

26
00:02:06,055 --> 00:02:09,399
Item by item, the adapters win and never lose.

27
00:02:09,399 --> 00:02:15,506
The negative control collapses to two percent, which is exactly why the gate exists.

28
00:02:16,706 --> 00:02:22,423
And the specialized model answers about ten times faster, without a long reasoning preamble.

29
00:02:23,706 --> 00:02:25,605
Three levels of evolution.

30
00:02:25,605 --> 00:02:29,256
Level one, prompt evolution in the spirit of GEPA:

31
00:02:29,256 --> 00:02:31,228
proposed, not yet measured.

32
00:02:31,228 --> 00:02:32,908
Level two, fine tuning:

33
00:02:32,908 --> 00:02:36,048
one LoRA per tenant, measured and promoted.

34
00:02:36,048 --> 00:02:38,678
Level three, reinforcement learning:

35
00:02:38,678 --> 00:02:44,228
today it is verifier corrected fine tuning, and policy gradient R L is next.

36
